  "problem": "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nTo make a delicious soup, Alice requires $3$ grams of ginger powder and $4$ grams of garlic powder, among other ingredients, so she needs $\\boxed{}$ grams of ginger powder for each gram of garlic.",
  "worked_solution": "The ratio of the number of grams of ginger powder to the number of grams of garlic powder is  $3:4.$ \n\nWe can rewrite this ratio as a fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nThis means that there is $\\frac{3}{4}$ grams of ginger powder for each gram of garlic powder.",
